XFAIL: system-windows, debug-build

Starting a program that does not exist fails to start it, under catter as
directly: build tools and shells rely on that error ("command not found",
trying the next candidate).
Known failures: #152 on Windows and #137 in debug builds.

RUN: %e2e probe missing-program | FileCheck %s
RUN: %catter script::cdb -q -o %t.json -- %e2e probe missing-program | FileCheck %s

CHECK: PASS missing-program
